BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Research Talks featuring Dr. Sugandha Gaur
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T180000
UID:research-talks-featuring-dr-sugandha-gaur@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the November edition of Research Talks\, featuring
  Dr. Sugandha Gaur with Guest Speaker Angela Bains. In this talk - “Adve
 rtising Futures: a community-interest industry" Dr. Gaur asks What if the 
 way we approach advertising considered capital as a tool for social transf
 ormation?\n\nJoin us for the November edition of Research Talks featuring 
 Dr. Sugandha Gaur presenting Advertising Futures: a community-interest ind
 ustry What if the way we approach advertising considered capital as a tool
  for social transformation? With Guest Speaker Angela Bains Brief Descript
 ion of the talk: This talk explores the work of the Advertising Action Col
 lective \, a research-led initiative that prepares creatives as advertisin
 g actionists reimagining a socially responsive industry. Further\, it prop
 oses stakeholders\, i.e.\, academia\, brands\, industry\, and consumers\, 
 an opportunity to investigate and implement alternative frameworks for col
 lective action by positioning capital not only as an economic resource but
  also as a tool for positive social impact. Through a series of "What if?"
  questions\, this session will encourage attendees to reassess traditional
  advertising approaches and imagine community-interest creative futures. A
 ngela bains has been a contributor to the work Sugandha has been creating 
 for Advertising Action Collective. Together\, they have contributed to the
  FLOW transformation within the program\, aligning ADVR program learnings 
 with Indigenous Learning Outcomes and decolonial pedagogies through their 
 collaborative work and shared experiences. Angela\, who is currently the C
 hair of the program\, is continuing to explore meaningful ways to embed th
 e Advertising Action Collective into the curriculum\, while extending its 
 impact beyond the classroom. The larger vision is to engage industry and b
 rands in this work and create opportunities for meaningful participation a
 nd collaboration among all stakeholders involved. Speaker Bio: Sugandha Ga
 ur\, Ph.D. (they/them) Associate Professor | Advertising Actionist\, Facul
 ty of Design Dr. Sugandha Gaur is an Advertising Actionist whose work span
 s education\, research\, and artistic practice. With over fifteen years of
  experience\, they focus on transforming ideas into collective action. Hol
 ding a Ph.D. in Media Arts\, Sugandha brings a strong foundation in creati
 ve and unconventional communication strategies to address complex social a
 nd environmental challenges. Their work is grounded in a commitment to lan
 d-based pedagogies and the recognition of Indigenous knowledges\, guided b
 y a belief in creativity as a catalyst for care and collective transformat
 ion. They are currently an Associate Professor in the Advertising Program 
 at OCAD University\, where they teach across all four years and lead the A
 dvertising Action Collective— a research-led initiative that prepares cr
 eatives as advertising actionists\, reimagining a socially responsive indu
 stry. It is a space that proposes an opportunity for stakeholders\, i.e.\,
  academia\, brands\, industry\, to investigate and implement alternative f
 rameworks for collective action by positioning capital not only as an econ
 omic resource but also as a tool for positive social impact. Through this 
 space\, their goal is for all the stakeholders to reassess traditional adv
 ertising approaches and imagine community-interest creative futures.\n\nGu
 est Speaker: Angela Bains Advertising Program Chair | Faculty of Design As
 sociate Professor Director\, Centre for Local Innovation & Collaboration (
 OCAD University) Special Advisor to the VP of Research: Innovation\, Outre
 ach\, & Commercialisation\n\nMicrosoft Teams meeting Join: https://teams.m
 icrosoft.com/meet/221631360770329?p=eDP3o8Z8DsCrqtpMkW Meeting ID: 221 631
  360 770 329 Passcode: Sz27kb9r This event is part of the Research Talks s
 eries organized by the Office of Research and Innovation\, and is free to 
 attend for everyone. For more information on the event or if you would lik
 e to present your work in this series\, feel free to reach out to tavleenl
 all@ocadu.ca or research@ocadu.ca Date and Time: Wednesday\, November 4\, 
 4 - 6 p.m. Location: Room 322 - 230 Richmond St W. Office of Research & In
 novation OCAD University Instagram: ocadu_research email: research@ocadu.c
 a
LOCATION:230 Richmond (RHB) 230 Richmond St. W Room 322
URL:https://teams.microsoft.com/meet/221631360770329?p=eDP3o8Z8DsCrqtpMkW
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
